r find the work done or explain why there is not enough data."] [#edb/ref 17592186672308 #edb/ref 17592186672329 "Source question: Problem 2(a)–(c), PDF page 3.\n\nAn object moves in the given force field from the initial point to the terminal point. Either find the work done or explain why there is not enough data."] [#edb/ref 17592186672376 #edb/ref 17592186672329 "Source question: Problem 2(a)–(c), PDF page 3.\n\nAn object moves in the given force field from the initial point to the terminal point. Either find the work done or explain why there is not enough data."] [#edb/ref 17592186672121 #edb/ref 17592186672331 "Source question: Problem 1(a)–(d), PDF page 2.\n\nFor each statement, explain why it is true or why it is false."] [#edb/ref 17592186672322 #edb/ref 17592186672331 "Source question: Problem 1(a)–(d), PDF page 2.\n\nFor each statement, explain why it is true or why it is false."] [#edb/ref 17592186672343 #edb/ref 17592186672331 "Source question: Problem 1(a)–(d), PDF page 2.\n\nFor each statement, explain why it is true or why it is false."] [#edb/ref 17592186672414 #edb/ref 17592186672331 "Source question: Problem 1(a)–(d), PDF page 2.\n\nFor each statement, explain why it is true or why it is false."] [#edb/ref 17592186672210 #edb/ref 17592186672347 "Source question: Problem 3(a)–(b), PDF page 4.\n\nLet $R$ be any region in the plane not containing the origin. The source’s requested assertions are preserved below."] [#edb/ref 17592186672301 #edb/ref 17592186672347 "Source question: Problem 3(a)–(b), PDF page 4.\n\nLet $R$ be any region in the plane not containing the origin. The source’s requested assertions are preserved below."] [#edb/ref 17592186672056 #edb/ref 17592186672349 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 8](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_2/8).\n\nA Bernoulli equation has the form $y\\prime+P(x)y=Q(x)y^n$. It is linear when n=0 or n=1. Otherwise, the substitution $u=y^{1-n}$ gives $u\\prime+(1-n)P(x)u=(1-n)Q(x)$.\n\nConsider $xy\\prime+y=-9xy^2$, y(1)=2."] [#edb/ref 17592186672107 #edb/ref 17592186672349 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 8](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_2/8).\n\nA Bernoulli equation has the form $y\\prime+P(x)y=Q(x)y^n$. It is linear when n=0 or n=1. Otherwise, the substitution $u=y^{1-n}$ gives $u\\prime+(1-n)P(x)u=(1-n)Q(x)$.\n\nConsider $xy\\prime+y=-9xy^2$, y(1)=2."] [#edb/ref 17592186672176 #edb/ref 17592186672349 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 8](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_2/8).\n\nA Bernoulli equation has the form $y\\prime+P(x)y=Q(x)y^n$. It is linear when n=0 or n=1. Otherwise, the substitution $u=y^{1-n}$ gives $u\\prime+(1-n)P(x)u=(1-n)Q(x)$.\n\nConsider $xy\\prime+y=-9xy^2$, y(1)=2."] [#edb/ref 17592186672312 #edb/ref 17592186672349 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 8](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_2/8).\n\nA Bernoulli equation has the form $y\\prime+P(x)y=Q(x)y^n$. It is linear when n=0 or n=1. Otherwise, the substitution $u=y^{1-n}$ gives $u\\prime+(1-n)P(x)u=(1-n)Q(x)$.\n\nConsider $xy\\prime+y=-9xy^2$, y(1)=2."] [#edb/ref 17592186672429 #edb/ref 17592186672349 "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 8](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_2/8).\n\nA Bernoulli equation has the form $y\\prime+P(x)y=Q(x)y^n$. It is linear when n=0 or n=1. Otherwise, the substitution $u=y^{1-n}$ gives $u\\prime+(1-n)P(x)u=(1-n)Q(x)$.\n\nConsider $xy\\prime+y=-9xy^2$, y(1)=2."] [#edb/ref 17592186672179 #edb/ref 17592186672367 "Source question: Problem 4(a)–(c), PDF page 5.\n\nEvaluate each integral using your method of choice. Show your supporting work."] [#edb/ref 17592186672214 #edb/ref 17592186672367 "Source question: Problem 4(a)–(c), PDF page 5.\n\nEvaluate each integral using your method of choice. Show your supporting work."] [#edb/ref 17592186672404 #edb/ref 17592